    {
      "srr_row": 473,
      "rule_id": "DAP-37",
      "statement": "A fine-tuned artefact MAY be pruned — magnitude pruning or an equivalent structural reduction — between MOAC acceptance and DAP-31's distance gate, as a ruled optional step. Pruning is a second, empirical reduction in memorisation surface on top of DAP-36's differentially private training; it is never a substitute for it, and this document does not present it as one. A pruned artefact MUST re-pass MOAC's acceptance criteria — pruning can degrade performance below the accepted bar, and acceptance is re-evaluated, not assumed to survive the change. A pruned artefact's hash differs from its pre-pruning hash; it is a new artefact for every purpose DAP-10 and DAP-31 govern, including a fresh pass through the distance gate at the ruled threshold. Pruning ratio and method are ruled values, ratified alongside DAP-31's own probe parameters.",
      "objective": "O13 Data & Intelligence Acquisition",
      "promise": "Pruning & Unlearning Amendment",
      "doc": "Pruning & Unlearning Amendment",
      "status": "PROPOSED",
      "enforcement_class": null,
      "domain": "O13 Data & Intelligence Acquisition",
      "source_file_line": "Pruning & Unlearning Amendment",
      "relationship": "Added at refresh 18 Sep 2026 — new, not in 444 baseline"
    },
    {
      "srr_row": 474,
      "rule_id": "DAP-38",
      "statement": "When a unit's rights status changes to withdrawn — consent revoked, licence expired, or an equivalent event — every artefact whose training manifest cites that unit is identified via the registry (a query, per RBM-20's design, not a search) and is either re-derived without the unit or recalled. Re-derivation trains a replacement artefact excluding the withdrawn unit, using the same run configuration recorded in the original training manifest, and passes it through DAP-31 and MOAC as a new artefact before it replaces the original in the registry. Recall withdraws the original artefact's registry entry and, where the artefact was already delivered under DAP-10, notifies the receiving party that the artefact's rights basis has changed. A unit's contribution to the estate release budget (DAP-35) is NOT refunded on unlearning — the privacy loss from the original release already occurred; unlearning restores the artefact's cleanliness going forward, not the budget already spent.",
      "objective": "O13 Data & Intelligence Acquisition",
      "promise": "Pruning & Unlearning Amendment",
      "doc": "Pruning & Unlearning Amendment",
      "status": "PROPOSED",
      "enforcement_class": null,
      "domain": "O13 Data & Intelligence Acquisition",
      "source_file_line": "Pruning & Unlearning Amendment",
      "relationship": "Added at refresh 18 Sep 2026 — new, not in 444 baseline"
